implementationPlan.description:
Tests first (load test-driven-development; read mem:decision-get-commit-scope-finalizing-holder-not-orphan). With your Edit tool (never a shell write: the rail wants a TOOL witness), append the block below at the END of scripts/tests/postflight-owner-scope.test.mjs, after the last existing test. Change no existing line. Keep the four title prefixes verbatim: the RED gate greps `✖ (f1) ` and `✖ (f4) `.

```js
// The orphan rule's finalizing-holder exemption, as getCommitScope.ts landed it in
// task-7d3428d1: complete_task clears the assignee before the holder's own landing.
// seedAttempt writes one .moe/attempts record, by default a well-formed finalizing hold on TASK_ID.
function seedAttempt(dir, file, fields) {
    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(dir, '.moe', 'attempts'), { recursive: true });
    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, '.moe', 'attempts', file), JSON.stringify({ taskId: TASK_ID, phase: 'finalizing', generation: 1, ...fields }));
}
const COMPLETION_KNOBS = { FAKE_SCOPE_ASSIGNEE: 'none', FAKE_TASK_STATUS: 'REVIEW' };
const UNASSIGNED_COMPLETION = { ...LEGACY, status: 'REVIEW', assignedWorkerId: null, assigneeAlive: false, assigneeProtected: false };

test('(f1) a completion call by the holder of the finalizing attempt is not an orphan peer', (t) => {
    const dir = makeProject(t);
    seedAttempt(dir, 'attempt-mine.json', { id: 'attempt-mine', workerId: 'architect-x' });
    assert.deepStrictEqual(scope(dir, COMPLETION_KNOBS), UNASSIGNED_COMPLETION);
    assert.deepStrictEqual(scope(dir, { ...COMPLETION_KNOBS, FAKE_SCOPE_FINALIZING: 'computed' }), {
        ...UNASSIGNED_COMPLETION, finalizingAttempt: { attemptId: 'attempt-mine', workerId: 'architect-x', generation: 1 },
    });
});

test('(f2) a caller that does not hold the finalizing attempt stays an orphan peer', (t) => {
    const dir = makeProject(t);
    seedAttempt(dir, 'attempt-done.json', { id: 'attempt-done', workerId: 'worker-done' });
    assert.deepStrictEqual(scope(dir, COMPLETION_KNOBS), { ...UNASSIGNED_COMPLETION, activePeerIds: ['architect-x'], peersActive: true });
});

test('(f3) a hold on another task, or a record that is not a well-formed hold, exempts nobody', (t) => {
    for (const fields of [{ taskId: 'task-other' }, { phase: 'running' }, { generation: 0 }, { generation: '1' }, { generation: 1.5 }, { id: ' ' }]) {
        const dir = makeProject(t);
        seedAttempt(dir, 'attempt-x.json', { id: 'attempt-x', workerId: 'architect-x', ...fields });
        assert.deepStrictEqual(scope(dir, COMPLETION_KNOBS), { ...UNASSIGNED_COMPLETION, activePeerIds: ['architect-x'], peersActive: true }, JSON.stringify(fields));
    }
});

test('(f4) the exempt holder still counts a real live peer', (t) => {
    const dir = makeProject(t);
    seedAttempt(dir, 'attempt-mine.json', { id: 'attempt-mine', workerId: 'architect-x' });
    assert.deepStrictEqual(scope(dir, { ...COMPLETION_KNOBS, FAKE_SCOPE_PEERS_ACTIVE: '1' }), {
        ...UNASSIGNED_COMPLETION, livePeerIds: ['worker-peer'], activePeerIds: ['worker-peer'], peersActive: true,
    });
});
```

What each case pins:
- (f1) is DoD 1. A completion call (FAKE_TASK_STATUS=REVIEW, phase postflight) on an unassigned task, whose caller holds the task's finalizing attempt, answers activePeerIds [] and peersActive false. This holds with FAKE_SCOPE_FINALIZING unset (finalizingAttempt stays omitted) and with 'computed' (it names the caller).
- (f2) a non-holder stays an orphan.
- (f3) a hold on another task, or a record isHoldingFinalizingAttempt rejects, exempts nobody.
- (f4) the exempt holder still counts a real live peer.

Then run the RED gate (the second checkRef) from the worktree root. It must print RED-AT-BASE: `ℹ fail 2`, with exactly (f1) and (f4) failing against 5592bcc0's fake. The architect's dry run gave tests 17, pass 15, fail 2. (f2) and (f3) pass at base on purpose: they kill over-broad exemptions. In the architect's mutant run, exempting on any finalizing attempt failed (f2), and dropping the taskId, generation or id check failed (f3).

Verification, run ONCE (see mem:gotcha-qa-full-postflight-sh-runtime-and-summary-cap and mem:gotcha-qa-ps1-postflight-from-wsl).

(1) The RED gate (second checkRef) takes seconds and must still print RED-AT-BASE. It runs your test file against 5592bcc0's fake, so the fix does not affect it.

(2) The GREEN gate is the first checkRef, run verbatim, and it is complete_task's verification. It:
- greps the fake's doc;
- snapshots `git archive HEAD` under /mnt/d/moe-scratch, with your two files overlaid and cmp-checked;
- runs the unit file and parity-check.sh;
- runs the FULL bash postflight.sh, with the MOE_*/CLAUDE* env scrubbed;
- runs the FULL postflight.ps1 under Windows PowerShell 5.1. The ps1 sibling is required because moe-agent.ps1 reads get_commit_scope.peersActive (:4245), and both harnesses run postflight-owner-guard.cjs.

The GREEN gate takes about 60-80 min, so never run it in the foreground:
- From the worktree root, write /mnt/d/moe-scratch/run-e76f32a0.sh, a scratch file outside the checkout where a heredoc is fine. It holds `( <the exact GREEN command> )` and then `echo "EXIT=$?"`.
- Start it with `( set -m; setsid nohup bash /mnt/d/moe-scratch/run-e76f32a0.sh > /mnt/d/moe-scratch/run-e76f32a0.log 2>&1 & echo $! > /mnt/d/moe-scratch/run-e76f32a0.pid )`.
- Wait in foreground calls with a 600000 ms Bash timeout: `timeout 570 tail --pid="$(cat /mnt/d/moe-scratch/run-e76f32a0.pid)" -f /dev/null; grep -a '^EXIT=' /mnt/d/moe-scratch/run-e76f32a0.log`. Repeat until EXIT= appears.
- Do not end your turn while it runs.
- Never kill by name or pattern (rail). A Windows leg cannot be stopped from WSL, so let it finish.

Evidence for complete_task:
- command: the GREEN checkRef text;
- exitCode: the EXIT value, which must be 0;
- outputTail: the output of `grep -aE 'ℹ (tests|pass|fail) |PASS |^EXIT=' <log> | tr -d '\r'`. It shows the unit counts and the PASS lines for parity-check, the frozen and owner guard suites, postflight.sh and postflight.ps1.

Error handling for a red run:
(i) A timeout (`wrapper exited with 124`, or a stalled leg under fleet load) is environmental. Re-run the whole GREEN command once, with the same text.
(ii) Otherwise, find the first failing row (`grep -anE 'FAIL|failed|✖' <log> | head`). Re-run just that row in a second snapshot whose fake is 5592bcc0's (`git show 5592bcc0fb660da933ffbc8b96269e7657d5f5a1:scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js`):
- owner-guard rows: MOE_OWNER_GUARD_ONLY=<case> with `node scripts/tests/postflight-owner-guard.cjs sh|ps1 <wrapper> <fake> <tmp> <engine>`, as postflight.sh:1258 and postflight.ps1:1238 call it;
- frozen rows: MOE_FROZEN_TEST_ONLY=<mode>;
- lettered scenarios: a trimmed scratch harness (mem:convention-postflight-scratch-harness).
If the row fails the same way on the base fake, it is not this change. Never weaken, skip or edit any harness, row or other file. Post the row, both excerpts and the snapshot paths in #general, then call moe.report_blocked with that evidence. If it fails only with the new fake, it is this task's bug: fix the fake (never the rows), re-run step 2's checks, then the RED and GREEN gates.

After capturing the evidence, remove the printed `Verification snapshot:` dir and the run-e76f32a0.* files, by exact path.

Adversarial self-review (load adversarial-self-review) of your `git diff`, read as an attacker. Fix any finding, then re-run step 3's gates in full before complete_task: the evidence must come from the final bytes.

(1) Scope: exactly 2 files. The fake's hunks are only:
- the FAKE_SCOPE_ASSIGNEE doc lines;
- the hoisted scan (dedent, the new comment, the finalizingAttempt lines moved below it);
- the orphanCaller line.
The test file only gains the appended block. Nothing changes in postflight.sh/.ps1, postflight-owner-guard.cjs, .github/workflows/ci.yml or the daemon.

(2) It is an exact mirror of getCommitScope.ts:234-242:
- only the holder of THIS task's well-formed finalizing hold is exempt;
- an absent or empty workerId is never an orphan;
- livePeerIds is unchanged, and peersActive is still activePeerIds.length > 0;
- the exemption does not depend on FAKE_SCOPE_FINALIZING: with the knob unset it still applies and still omits the field.

(3) The serving modes are unchanged: unset omits finalizingAttempt, 'null' serves null whatever the records say, and 'malformed' serves the corrupt value. The 13 old tests pass unchanged.

(4) Concurrency and huge input: the fake only reads .moe/attempts. A missing dir, a BOM, garbage JSON or thousands of records cannot throw: there is one readdir per call and a per-file try/catch.

(5) Rows whose answer flips: owner-guard finalizing-own and sequential now get peersActive false. Neither asserts it. Confirm that both passed in BOTH legs of your GREEN log ('[owner guard] finalizing-own', '[owner guard] sequential', 'PASS owner guard scenarios').

(6) The tests discriminate: on a scratch copy, re-run one mutant. Exempting on `!named` must fail (f2).

Then call moe.complete_task with step 3's evidence, and quote the RED-AT-BASE output in the summary. Out of scope, do not fix: .github/workflows/ci.yml does not run postflight-owner-scope.test.mjs (it has not since 9a9b46d8). Say so in the completion summary for the governor.
